@group
    @title=CS2DS template
    @brief=The section describes the template that creates a documentation source using output of Assembly2Xml task and xml docs.
    @ingroup=templates
    @key=cs2dsTemplate

    To prepare the source data about content of assembly or assemblies
    to auto-document, use [clink=msbuildTasks.Asm2Xml]Asm2Xml[/clink]
    task. This task would create a source file for the processing.

    Please not that this assembly does NOT use [link=modelXML]DocGen XML document[/link]
    as a source. It opens and processes the document specified
    in the template parameters. However, because it is still required to have
    any DocGen XML document, you have to create a source file with an
    empty index group, e.g. and specify it as a source for your
    [link=docProjectFile]docgen project[/link].

    @example
        @show=always
        @gray=yes
    !@group
    !    @title=Index
    !    @brief=
    !    @key=index
    !    @ingroup=
    !@end
    @end

    The template is located at
    `%docgen%/template/cs2ds/main.xsl`

    This template creates multiple output files, so use `file` parameter
    of the [clink=docProjectFile1.output]output[/clink] element of the project file
    to specify the destination folder:

    Example:

    ```xml
    <dg:output template="%docgen%/template/cs2ds/main.xsl" file="src/raw/null-file" encoding="utf-8">
    ```

    The template has following parameters:

    @table
        @row
            @header=yes
            @col
                @width=30%
                Parameter
            @end
            @col
                Description
            @end
        @end

        @row
            @col
                `settings`
            @end
            @col
                The path to file with XML file with additional settings.
            @end
        @end

        @row
            @col
                `source`
            @end
            @col
                The name of the source file
                generated by `Asm2Xml` task.
            @end
        @end

        @row
            @col
                `default-group`
            @end
            @col
                The template will create
                a group for each namespace processed.

                All these groups will belong to the group
                specified in this key. Usually the
                value of this parameter is `index`, however
                more complex documentation may require
                to attach auto-generated content to a
                specific node in the content tree.
            @end
        @end
    @end
@end

@class
    @name=Settings File Schema
    @key=cs2dsTemplateSettings
    @brief=
    @ingroup=cs2dsTemplate
    @type=tags

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=settings
        @brief=The root element of the settings file.
        @custom=xml-tag

        The element may contain one or more
        [clink=cs2dsTemplateSettings.assembly]assembly[/clink]
        and
        [clink=cs2dsTemplateSettings.strip-namespace]strip-namespace[/clink]
        elements.
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=assembly
        @brief=The assembly to be processed
        @custom=xml-tag

        The element defines the assembly to be processed.

        @param
            @name=name
            The name of the assembly without `.dll` extension.
        @end

        @param
            @name=xmldoc
            The path to the XML Doc file generated by C# compiler
            from source code comments. The path specified must be
            relative to a location of the assembly file
            from which the source XML document is generated.

            This value is optional. If no XML doc location is set,
            the documentation will be generated for the structure,
            without any descriptions included.
        @end
    @end

    @member
        @type=property
        @name=strip-namespace
        @brief=The list of namespaces those names should be displayed as a short name rather than full name
        @custom=xml-tag

        @param
            @name=name
            The name of namespace.
        @end

        The types to belong to the assembly specified will be
        shown in the documentation using their short names rather than
        full names.

        The following areas will be affected:
        * The list of class parents
        * The types of the parameters in declarations
        * The return types in the declarations

        E.g. by default an auto-generated declaration may look like these

        ```csharp
        System.Task<System.Collections.Generic.List<T>> Sample<T>(System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable<T> parameter);
        ```

        If you add the following lines to the project file

        ```xml
        <settings>
         ...
         <strip-namespace name="System" />
         <strip-namespace name="System.Collections.Generic" />
         ...
        </settings>
        ```

        The declaration will look like this

        ```csharp
        Task<List<T>> Sample<T>(IEnumerable<T> parameter);
        ```
    @end
@end
